+{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_0123GRv5Gj5vC62qByKnboCa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015ATvJc7pDBXdupGiY7tXhU","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/workspace/CONTRACT.md","content":"# Spreadsheet Engine Contract\n\n## Behaviors\n\n### Cell References\n1. Cells are referenced by uppercase column letter(s) + 1-based row number: A1, Z100, AA1\n2. Column numbering: A=1, Z=26, AA=27, AZ=52, BA=53, ...\n3. Cell refs passed to set/get are normalized to uppercase\n\n### Raw Value Storage\n4. `set(cell, number)` stores a number, `get` returns that number\n5. `set(cell, boolean)` stores a boolean, `get` returns that boolean\n6. `set(cell, \"non-formula string\")` stores a string, `get` returns that string\n7. `get` returns null for any cell that has never been set\n\n### Formula Evaluation\n8. `set(cell, \"=expr\")` evaluates the formula and stores its result\n9. Arithmetic: +, -, *, / with standard precedence (* / before + -)\n10. Parentheses override precedence: =(2+3)*4 → 20\n11. Unary minus: =-A1 negates the value\n12. Cell references in formulas resolve to the cell's computed value (null cells resolve to null/0)\n13. String literals in formulas use double quotes: =\"hello\"\n14. Boolean literals: =TRUE, =FALSE (case-insensitive)\n15. Comparison operators: >, <, >=, <=, =, <> return boolean\n16. Comparisons have lower precedence than arithmetic\n\n### Built-in Functions\n17. SUM(range) returns sum of all numeric values in range (ignores non-numeric)\n18. AVERAGE(range) returns arithmetic mean of numeric values; 0 if no numerics\n19. MIN(range) returns smallest numeric value; 0 if no numerics\n20. MAX(range) returns largest numeric value; 0 if no numerics\n21. COUNT(range) returns count of numeric values\n22. IF(cond, trueVal, falseVal) returns trueVal when cond is truthy, falseVal otherwise\n\n### Ranges\n23. Column range A1:A5 → A1, A2, A3, A4, A5\n24. Row range A1:C1 → A1, B1, C1\n